Our refund processing dashboard has a bug. When an agent clicks the 'Submit Refund' button, it's supposed to get disabled to prevent duplicate submissions, but it's not working reliably. It seems to fail if the API call throws an error. Here's the broken JavaScript function. Can you fix it so the button is always re-enabled after the fetch completes, whether it succeeds or fails? 

```javascript
async function processRefund(ticketId, refundAmount) {
  const refundBtn = document.getElementById(`refund-btn-${ticketId}`);
  refundBtn.innerText = 'Processing...';
  refundBtn.disabled = true;

  const response = await fetch('/api/internal/v1/refunds', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ ticket: ticketId, amount: refundAmount })
  });

  if (response.ok) {
    showConfirmation('Refund processed successfully!');
  } else {
    showError('Refund failed. Please check logs.');
    // The button stays disabled on error!
  }
}
```

